WEBVTT

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:31.720
<i>Suteta hazu no fuan no tane ga 
kokoro tsukiyabutte me o dashita</i>

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:47.950
<i>Musuu no ibara ga kyou mo 
ashimoto nobite machikamaeteiru</i>

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:56.410
<i>Doko e yukeba aeru</i>

00:00:56.410 --> 00:01:11.300
<i>Dakishimenaide senaka no toge 
wa kimi o kizutsukeru yo</i>

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:26.530
<i>Soredemo afureru omoi ga kimi o sagashiteiru</i>

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:36.400
"Nessa"

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:36.400
Miss Phryne! Miss Phryne!

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.410
Oh, Miss Phryne... Where'd she go?

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:41.280
Calm down.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.080
Archpriestess!

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:44.820
"Where'd she go"?

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.930
That's a funny question.

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:49.880
She cannot go anywhere.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:53.050
Everything is connected in this world.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:55.560
When she comes back,

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:59.010
she needs to be punished severely.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:02.100
To think that she stole 
the key to the world...

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:04.720
Tada!

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:14.730
Who are you?

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:16.860
U... U... Um...

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:20.880
Oh, Nessa's sorry. Nessa 
forgot to bid you greetings.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.640
Good morning!

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:26.410
So, who are you?

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.460
Clain...

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.840
It's a new morning!

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.810
Good morning, Clain!

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:37.640
Say...

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:39.360
Yes?

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.930
You are... a doppel, right?

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:43.430
Hm?

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:47.000
But for a doppel, you sure look real.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.400
Do you wanna try patting Nessa's head?

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.450
Don’t hold back. Here, Nessa's head!

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:01.950
I can feel it!

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.730
Right? It's mysterious, isn't it?

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:07.220
Nessa doesn't know much about Nessa, either.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.460
Nessa is mysterious, isn't she?

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:10.650
Nessa?

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:11.500
Nessa!

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.130
Anyway, what's your relationship with Phryne?

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.280
Phryne?

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:16.820
You don't know her?

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:19.130
She's the girl who left you here, right?

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.260
She left Nessa here?

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:28.020
This Phryne person... Does she dislike Nessa?

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:31.600
What?! Well, I don't think that's the case.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.270
Then, Nessa's relieved!

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.780
Nessa dislikes disliking.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:41.130
Nessa likes liking!

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:51.540
♪ If I am to offer a wish 
to the day star... ♪

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:53.920
<i>So she isn't... Phryne's doppel?</i>...

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.290
♪ I would ask it to let me be ♪

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:58.710
<i>She's a somewhat fickle, strange girl. </i>...

00:03:55.290 --> 00:04:00.180
♪ good friends with Clain. ♪

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:02.230
<i>Well, Phryne is strange, too, I guess. </i>...

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:05.640
Good morning!

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.350
Clain! You brought home another girl?!

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:12.390
It's not like that!

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.440
This is something the girl 
from yesterday left behind.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.610
Something she left behind? You mean...

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.070
Whoa! How cute!

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.450
<i>She can touch a doppel?</i>

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:28.350
You're right... She isn't... a human.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:30.910
I told you... This is something 
that girl left behind.

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:33.040
Then you should return this to her.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:33.870
What?!

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:37.080
If you can't do that, then 
bring it to the police.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.100
B-But...

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.330
This is something she left 
behind, right? Then...

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.750
Clain!

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:45.380
Look! This is a huge ribbon!

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:53.390
<i>Even if I want to return this, 
I don't know where Phryne is.</i>

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:02.280
Whoa...! There are some 
birds! They look happy.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:05.090
Nessa likes birds.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:07.740
Say, do you think Phryne likes birds, too?

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.170
How should I know?!

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.280
<i>Phryne, huh?</i>

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.040
<i>What do I wanna do when I see her?</i>

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:16.960
<i>For starters, I wanna give her an earful.</i>

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:18.880
<i>I'll give her an earful!</i>

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.760
The wind feels good!

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:29.090
It hits Nessa's cheeks! 
It hits Nessa's cheeks!

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:33.610
Don't move so much, or you'll fall.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:36.480
Nessa!

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.410
See, I told you!

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:48.520
But, well, you're a doppel, 
so you're okay, right?

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:52.080
H-Hey...

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.330
Clain...

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:55.830
Touch Nessa.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.750
Touch you? Why?

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:00.940
Touch Nessa.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.560
You're touching Nessa. You're touching Nessa.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.720
Wh-What's the big deal?

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.070
You're touching Nessa.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:29.700
Hmm? This place seems kinda crestfallen.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.750
It's very quiet.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:35.120
Ah! Nessa found a man!

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:40.250
You really don't know anything, do you?

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:43.210
This area just has some facilities.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:45.640
Security, government office and such...

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:50.050
The buildings remain, but not 
so many people live around here.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:51.010
Really?

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:55.510
Nessa, there's no point in 
you staying at my place.

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:58.340
So... maybe... here would be...

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:03.860
Whoa! What a big clock!

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:09.360
Nessa!

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:19.160
Ding, dong, ding, dong...

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.330
Geez... don't go in there without permission!

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:27.090
Ding, dong, ding, dong...

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:28.800
Wait up, Nessa!

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.720
Whoa!

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:34.440
How beautiful!

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:43.800
There are lots of vehicles!

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:46.570
Are they here on vacation?

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:49.440
No, those mobiles are their houses.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:50.570
Huh?

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:53.530
I've heard that it's convenient, 
not being tied down to anything.

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:57.050
Plus, they can easily move 
whenever a star falls, too.

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:57.690
Star?

00:07:57.690 --> 00:07:59.120
I'm talking about the balloons.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:02.070
The radio waves are strong 
all around the town.

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:04.920
Not having a house probably 
makes people feel at ease.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:07.710
But you have a house.

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:11.800
Well, you see, I like old stuff, so...

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.930
Mom complains about it a lot, though.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:18.560
They're all lost, aren't they?

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:19.220
Huh?

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:22.980
None of them have a place 
they can call home, huh?

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:26.610
Even if they have a place they call home

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:29.220
the only ones waiting for them 
are doppels anyway, right?

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:32.990
They're not tied to anything from the start.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:34.450
If that's the case,

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:38.330
they're probably better off not 
being tied down to a house.

00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:40.710
Huuuuuuuh?!

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:46.080
She's too fast... Give me a break!

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:05.980
Nessa... Geez... She's already gone again!

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:07.980
Say, what're you watching?

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:18.890
Say, does it make you happier than 
being patted on the head by someone?

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:26.350
Whoa! So they sleep in here.

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:28.550
I wonder where the restroom is.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.710
Awww... It's gone.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:37.510
Oh no...

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:44.390
Hey, Nessa, listen.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:47.890
Look, look, Clain! The 
baby says he's having fun!

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:49.440
He's got dimples!

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:51.650
Like I said, Nessa...

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:52.900
Ahh... give me a break!

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:59.270
It flew! It flew!

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:03.790
They all look like they're having fun!

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:07.440
It's her fault! She's the one 
causing all this crazy nonsense!

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:13.460
Hey, you two, pay for the damages!

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:26.810
I've never been this stirred 
up by someone before.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:29.390
It was fun, wasn't it, Clain?!

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:31.560
Hey, where should we go next?

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:33.520
Security.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:34.270
What?

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:36.490
I'm going there to leave you in their hands!

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:38.240
I can't be with you anymore!

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:41.660
Why? Nessa will stay with you.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:42.450
Like I said...!

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:44.530
Because where you are is Nessa's home!

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:45.490
Your home?

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:48.980
You called Nessa out.

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:51.750
So where you are is Nessa's home.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:58.920
<i>I wonder why... Nessa's smile...</i>

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:02.430
<i>scares me...</i>

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:03.800
Clain?

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:05.760
Let's go.

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:15.900
You can't... touch Nessa anymore?

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:21.090
Let's go to Security.

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:22.530
Nessa...

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:31.210
Left behind? Well, we'll keep it 
here for the time being, but...

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.420
Sorry.

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.740
See you, Clain!

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.650
Serves you right!

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:54.310
Huh?

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:57.990
You stole some parts that 
belong to us, didn't you?!

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:02.030
It's payback. P-a-y-b-a-c-k...

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:03.450
You guys...

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:06.110
We'll take you in!

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:12.080
Yes, Sir!

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:13.920
What? What?!

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.830
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:17.130
Hey!

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:25.050
Big Brother!

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:26.510
We brought him in, Bro!

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:27.720
Here you go!

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:29.970
Wh-What's the deal?

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:32.390
So you're the one...

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:36.020
who was hiding that priestess...

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:36.920
What?

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:40.650
Say, Boy... Where's that woman?

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:42.820
I-I don't know.

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:44.740
She left somewhere early in the morning.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:47.200
Y-Y-You're so naughty!

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:47.660
Huh?

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:49.620
You were with her until morning?!

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:51.450
You are definitely naughty!

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:52.720
Sanitize him!

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:54.500
Yes, Sir!

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:57.080
Enri.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:05.900
I see...

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:07.390
Then, Boy...

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:12.100
You keep calling me "Boy," 
but you're a boy, too.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:15.390
That fuss earlier at the camping site...

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:17.600
You're the one who caused it, right?

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:20.770
It wasn't me. It was the 
doppel that Phryne had...

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:21.530
Yeah?

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:24.690
Ah... I-I don't know where it is now, though.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:27.910
It went somewhere... on its own.

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:29.780
Liar! I know you know!

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:34.250
You're naughty! So you 
must know this and that!

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:36.040
Quit calling me naughty!

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.000
You've got it all wrong!

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.420
You can go home.

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:40.460
Big Brother!

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:42.810
Well then...

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:45.890
In this world...

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:50.470
whether it's working or 
even moving your body,

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:54.470
doppels take care of everything 
that's troublesome for you.

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:56.320
But...

00:13:57.690 --> 00:14:03.110
the things that you experience for 
yourself are far more shocking.

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:05.220
Isn't that right, Boy?

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:07.740
I already knew that...

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:13.910
<i>He said I could go home...</i>

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:20.170
<i>but it's so obvious that I'm 
being followed, isn't it?</i>

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:24.610
<i>I wonder if they really 
think I don't notice them.</i>

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:34.400
<i>Oh well... Neither Phryne 
nor Nessa is here anyway...</i>

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:52.230
<i>Was this room always this big?</i>

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:59.810
<i>I don't have my own doppel.</i>

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:03.920
<i>I somehow didn't like the idea 
that there is another me.</i>

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:07.050
<i>So I don't want that guy to 
tell me things like that.</i>

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:11.760
Touchable... doppel... Search...

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:17.430
Oh, it's been developed already.

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:20.020
<i>So as I thought Nessa is...</i>

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:21.770
Let's see...

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:27.730
The calculator that depicts the doppel 
computes the pressure and effect, and...

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:33.110
What?! They're sold on the black 
market to be used as sex toys?!

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:37.160
This does make it look 
like I'm really naughty!

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:40.000
<i>However, in order to be able to touch them,</i>

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:42.580
<i>you need to transfer the target doppel's data</i>

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:45.170
<i>into the nanomachine inside your body, and...</i>

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:46.150
What?!

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:51.420
<i>Transfer data? I didn't 
do anything like that.</i>

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:52.950
Clain.

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:58.310
We want to talk to you. Have a seat.

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:04.730
Say, Clain. Let's not keep 
secrets from each other, okay?

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:05.440
Huh?

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:08.090
If you're worried about 
something, please tell us.

00:16:08.090 --> 00:16:11.490
Your father and I will help 
you figure things out...

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:12.820
What're you talking about?

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:21.910
We just get the feeling that you 
haven't been your usual self lately.

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:24.790
You go to suspicious places and... well...

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:27.480
you bring girls home.

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:29.030
Well, it's not like that. Phryne is...

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:35.370
Clain. Your father and I permit you 
to have a house because we trust you.

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:39.600
So we want you to be more 
aware of that, Clain.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:44.600
If you're so concerned about what I'm doing,

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:46.770
why don't you live here with me?

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:48.480
What're you saying?

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:50.730
If we do that, all of our 
freedoms will be restricted.

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:51.900
What?

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:55.950
Understanding each other deeply, 
indeed, is what allows us to be free.

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:59.090
That's how family is, right?

00:16:59.090 --> 00:17:02.080
To think a family would stay in one house...

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.250
That's just proof that there's 
no trust in the family.

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.710
You called Nessa out.

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:12.210
So where you are is Nessa's home.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.790
Also, you're so important to us.

00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:18.470
That's why we use our 
doppels like this and...

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:20.320
You make such lofty statements...

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:23.850
but it's really because you want 
everything to go your way, right?

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:26.770
Clain, you really are acting strange.

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:29.900
You never defied your father before.

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:31.270
Is that right?

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:32.190
Clain...

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:34.500
If it appears that way to you...

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:37.450
isn't it because your doppels are broken?

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:38.490
What?

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:55.340
<i>For some reason, it seems like 
I've been running all day.</i>

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:00.130
<i>It feels like something 
is about to burst out.</i>

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:03.220
<i>When I run like this,</i>

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:06.630
<i>it feels like something is about 
to burst out from my mouth.</i>

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:25.130
<i>I've become alone...</i>

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:29.670
<i>It's wrong to blame Mom and Dad.</i>

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:34.590
<i>I know that much.</i>

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:39.620
<i>Because I'd be bothered...</i>

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:43.100
<i>Because I'd be thrown off of my pace...</i>

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:46.660
<i>That's why I got rid of Nessa.</i>

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:55.590
It's time for the eight-o'clock prayer. 
The direction of the hovering...

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:55.590
Prayer, my ass.

00:18:56.480 --> 00:19:01.730
You're just taking my data, that's all.

00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:04.280
Now, let's offer a prayer.

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:05.030
<i>But...</i>

00:19:05.350 --> 00:19:13.000
♪ If I am to offer a wish 
to the day star... ♪

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:15.640
<i>My wish...</i>

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:21.200
<i>Is it that I wanna see Phryne?</i>

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:23.640
<i>Or is it that I wanna apologize to Nessa?</i>

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:26.270
<i>I don't know, but...</i>

00:19:27.210 --> 00:19:30.210
I don't want to... I don't want to be alone.

00:19:33.350 --> 00:19:34.770
Yoo-hoo!

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:38.570
Yoo-hoo!

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:41.070
Yoo-hoo! Yoo-hoo!

00:19:48.490 --> 00:19:49.250
Ooph!

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:52.670
<i>Nessa's smile...</i>

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:55.630
<i>isn't scary at all.</i>

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:01.840
Clain! Nessa's home!

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:06.800
<i>It isn't scary at all. On the contrary...</i>

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:08.560
Welcome home.

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:13.310
You're warm, Clain.

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:17.270
<i>That's my line.</i>

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:32.290
I wonder why those people make 
themselves so conspicuous.

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:36.940
Whoa! There's some treasure, Clain!

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:39.210
What?! Well... Hey, wait up!

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:47.050
Ow...

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:50.640
You fell for it, you fool!

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:53.690
I don't think I fell for it in this case...

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:55.600
They got us, didn't they?

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:58.680
Collect them, guys!

00:20:58.680 --> 00:21:00.050
Got it!

00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:01.670
Collect us?!

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:09.450
Whoa! We're flying!

00:21:15.570 --> 00:21:18.170
Go!
